          "source_quote": "ὁμῶς ταῦτα εἰπόντες προῆξαν",
          "english_quote": "Nevertheless, after saying this, they went ahead",
          "issue": "The selected edition prints ὁμῶς, not the usual adversative spelling ὅμως. The printed form admits the sense 'alike/together.' The draft supplies an adversative interpretation without identifying the printed accentuation or explaining whether it is treating that accentuation as an orthographic feature. This is a disclosure problem in verified print, not evidence of OCR corruption.",
          "suggested_revision": "Add a source-quoted note distinguishing the supplied ὁμῶς from ὅμως, explaining the grounds for retaining 'Nevertheless,' and preserving 'alike/together' as an alternative. Alternatively, submit 'After saying this together, they went ahead' for fresh review. Do not silently replace the supplied spelling.",
          "severity": "minor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "reference": "12.4",
      "verdict": "revise",
      "checks": {
        "complete_coverage": false,
